    {
      "id": "claim_2b042907286d4b0a8f0346d855f3dc6d",
      "statement": "step crypto registers change-pass, create-key-pair, jwk, jwt, jwe, jws, jose, hash, kdf, key, nacl, otp, rand, and winpe; its documented philosophy gates insecure primitives behind --insecure and delicate options behind --subtle, enforces 256-bit symmetric and 2048-bit RSA minimums, defaults EC to P-256 despite it not being a safe curve, and documents the rationale in SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS sections.",
